# iOS Navigation Standards

## Purpose

Define the expected pattern for adding screens, overlays, modal drawers, deeplink targets, and playback navigation in the existing iOS project.

## Current Project Pattern

- Root app flow lives under `App/DailyWire/App/Root`.
- Main tab/root flow lives under `App/DailyWire/UI/Main/Root`.
- Shared navigation support lives under `App/DailyWire/UI/Coordinator`.
- Deeplink parsing and routing support lives under `App/DailyWire/UI/Deeplinker`.
- Player and mini-player navigation are coordinated with media services under `App/DailyWire/UI/Player` and `App/DailyWire/Services/Media`.
- Some feature flows, such as Shorts, use their own scene/view model/coordinator pieces inside `Services/<feature>`.

## Required Standards

- Keep screen routing decisions in flow coordinators, navigation services, or view models that already own that flow.
- Do not navigate directly from reusable cards, rows, sheets, or shared UI components when a callback/action can be sent upward.
- Use the existing `Coordinator`, root flow, main flow, and deeplinker infrastructure before adding a new router or navigation abstraction.
- Keep modal sheets, drawers, popups, tooltips, and temporary panels as UI state unless they need root-level navigation, deeplink support, or their own back-stack behavior.
- Keep full-screen overlay experiences self-contained and explicit about close/back behavior.
- Pass screen identity through typed values such as slugs, IDs, domain models, or existing route targets rather than raw URL strings.
- Do not move a screen between root flow, main tab flow, player flow, and overlay flow unless the task explicitly requires a behavior change.
- Keep top bar, status bar, player visibility, and tab visibility updates close to the screen or flow that owns them.

## Choosing Where A Screen Belongs

- Add a screen to root flow when it is outside the main tab experience, controls app launch/auth/subscription gating, or should cover the current app context.
- Add a screen to main flow when it belongs inside the signed-in tab experience.
- Add a modal/drawer as local UI state when dismissal returns to the same screen and no route identity is needed.
- Add playback-only routing through media services when selecting content should play without opening a new detail screen.
- Add deeplink mapping only when external or stored URL input needs to open the screen.

## Do / Don't

Do:

```swift
FeatureCard(
    item: item,
    onSelect: { viewModel.send(.itemSelected(id: item.id)) }
)
```

Don't:

```swift
FeatureCard(item: item)
    .onTapGesture {
        appCoordinator.openFeature(slug: item.slug)
    }
```

Reason: reusable UI should not instantiate navigation dependencies or decide route ownership.

Do:

```swift
func send(_ action: FeatureAction) {
    switch action {
    case .itemSelected(let id):
        coordinator.openFeature(id: id)
    }
}
```

Don't:

```swift
func send(_ action: FeatureAction) {
    let id = "feature-id"
    UIApplication.shared.open(URL(string: "dailywire://feature/\(id)")!)
}
```

Reason: internal navigation should not round-trip through URL handling.

## Deeplinks

- URL parsing belongs in the deeplink layer.
- Deeplink-to-destination mapping belongs in deeplink/navigation helpers, not in screen UI.
- Playback-first deeplinks should route through media services rather than inventing fake screen destinations.
- Unsupported external URLs should fall back to browser handling when appropriate.

## Exceptions

- Existing legacy flows may use older coordinator patterns. Preserve local consistency for narrow bug fixes.
- UIKit representables may use local coordinators for delegate bridging; those coordinators should not become app routers.
- A one-off modal can stay local to a view if it has no route identity and no cross-screen reuse.

## Validation Expectations

- For navigation changes, verify source screen, destination screen, back behavior, tab/player visibility, and modal dismissal.
- For deeplink changes, add or update focused parser and routing tests.
- For playback routing changes, verify the media path and now-playing/miniplayer behavior.
- For overlay changes, verify the underlying tab/root state is preserved or reset intentionally.
